DOCS_FRAGMENT("education", "<div class=\"tldr pagecard\" data-page=\"education\"><div class=\"tldr-h\">In short</div><div class=\"cardrow\" data-field=\"what\" data-source=\"card\"><div class=\"cardk\">What it is</div><div class=\"cardv\"><p><code>Vzdělání</code> records a schooling itinerary, the schools a man attended with the years at each (<code>ob. 5 mě. 3 pok. 3</code>), not a level. It is parsed onto a six-rung ladder of the Cisleithanian school system under the 1869 law, recording attendance rather than attainment, with the apprentices' continuation school (<code>pok.</code>) off the ladder in a flag of its own. The ladder rests on two secondary works and the state's own school statistics of the 1908/1909 school year, and holds for Cisleithania</p></div></div><div class=\"cardrow\" data-field=\"numbers\"><div class=\"cardk\">The numbers that matter</div><div class=\"cardv\"><table class=\"cardnums nosort\"><tbody><tr><td>Records placed on a rung of the ladder</td><td class=\"num\"><span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"pf.legion.education.placed\" title=\"pf.legion.education.placed\">105,040</span></td></tr><tr><td>Elementary school as the highest rung, of all records</td><td class=\"num\"><span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"pf.legion.education.elementary.share\" title=\"pf.legion.education.elementary.share\">48.8 %</span></td></tr><tr><td>Burgher school as the highest rung, of all records</td><td class=\"num\"><span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"pf.legion.education.burgher_school.share\" title=\"pf.legion.education.burgher_school.share\">15.0 %</span></td></tr><tr><td>Name the continuation school (a lower bound on apprenticeship)</td><td class=\"num\"><span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"pf.legion.education_apprentice.share\" title=\"pf.legion.education_apprentice.share\">6.6 %</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"cardrow\" data-field=\"open\"><div class=\"cardk\">What's open</div><div class=\"cardv\"><span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"open.education.rulings\">3</span> rulings in this page's <i>Open for the author</i> table, each with what holds until you rule. <a href=\"#open\">What is open</a></div></div><div class=\"cardrow\" data-field=\"data\"><div class=\"cardk\">Where the data lives</div><div class=\"cardv\"><code>data/final/persons/legionnaires_clean.parquet</code> · key <code>legion_id</code> · <span class=\"tok\" data-token=\"mf.persons.legionnaires_clean.rows\">132,993</span> rows · columns <code>education*</code></div></div></div><div class=\"undercard\"><b>Decisions this page cites</b> <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-29\">D-29</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-33\">D-33</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-51\">D-51</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-276\">D-276</a> · <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-277\">D-277</a></div><nav class=\"toc parts\"><span>Sections</span><a href=\"#part-education\">Education ladder</a><a href=\"#validation-education\">External validation — education</a></nav><section class=\"part trunk\" id=\"part-education\" data-part=\"education\"><h2 class=\"parth\">Education ladder</h2><p class=\"lede partlede\">The 1869 Austrian school ladder — and why the apprentices&#x27; continuation school is not a rung on it. · source: <code>reference/EDUCATION_LADDER.md</code></p><nav class=\"toc\"><span>On this page</span><a href=\"#education-1-the-ladder-1869-1918\">1. The ladder, 1869–1918</a><a href=\"#education-2-the-vocational-branch-which-moore-does-not-reach\">2. The vocational branch, which Moore does not reach</a><a href=\"#education-2a-the-administration-s-own-taxonomy-1908-09\">2a. The administration&#x27;s own taxonomy (1908/09)</a><a href=\"#education-3-what-the-field-contains\">3. What the field contains</a><a href=\"#education-4-what-the-first-parser-got-wrong-v1-0-0\">4. What the first parser got wrong (v1.0.0)</a><a href=\"#education-5-what-is-still-open\">5. What is still open</a><a href=\"#education-6-the-revision-as-implemented-education-py-2-0-0-extended-in-2-1-0\">6. The revision, as implemented (education.py 2.0.0, extended in 2.1.0)</a><a href=\"#education-citation\">Citation</a><a href=\"#education-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</a><a href=\"#education-the-ladder-in-the-data\">The ladder in the data</a></nav><!-- card\nwhat: `Vzdělání` records a schooling itinerary, the schools a man attended with the years at each\n(`ob. 5 mě. 3 pok. 3`), not a level. It is parsed onto a six-rung ladder of the Cisleithanian school\nsystem under the 1869 law, recording attendance rather than attainment, with the apprentices'\ncontinuation school (`pok.`) off the ladder in a flag of its own. The ladder rests on two secondary\nworks and the state's own school statistics of the 1908/1909 school year, and holds for Cisleithania\nonly: the Slovak and Rusyn births ride on it unvalidated (D-08).\nnumber: pf.legion.education.placed | Records placed on a rung of the ladder\nnumber: pf.legion.education.elementary.share | Elementary school as the highest rung, of all records\nnumber: pf.legion.education.burgher_school.share | Burgher school as the highest rung, of all records\nnumber: pf.legion.education_apprentice.share | Name the continuation school (a lower bound on apprenticeship)\ndata: mf.persons.legionnaires_clean | education*\n-->\n\n<p><strong>Status.</strong> <code>utils/parsing/education.py</code> 2.1.0 builds the ladder: 2.0.0 rebuilt it on the sources below, and 2.1.0\nadded the tie-break, semesters and word anchoring (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-51\">D-51</a>). <code>schema.py</code> carries the columns. <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> stays <strong>Open</strong>, not\nbecause the code is unfinished, but because the ladder is established for <strong><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-cisleithania-en\" data-gl=\"cisleithania\">Cisleithania</a> only</strong> and the Hungarian half\nof the sample rides on it unvalidated (§5).</p>\n<p><strong>Sources.</strong> Three: two secondary works that divide the ladder between them, and — since 2026-09-07 — the primary\nsource that checks it.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"moore_2020\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Moore (2020)</a></strong>, <em>Teaching the Empire</em>: the <strong>general</strong> ladder (§1).</li>\n<li><strong><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"lassnigg_2015\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Lassnigg (2015)</a></strong>, IHS Sociological Series Working Paper 108: the <strong>vocational</strong> branch (§2).</li>\n<li><strong>k.k. Statistische Zentralkommission (1912)</strong>, <em>Österreichische Statistik</em> XCIII/1: the administration's <strong>own</strong>\n  taxonomy and counts (§2a).</li>\n</ul>\n<details><summary>The three sources in full, their files and how their pages are cited</summary>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Moore, Scott O. (2020).</b> <i>Teaching the Empire: Education and State Loyalty in Late Habsburg Austria.</i> West Lafayette: Purdue University Press (Central European Studies). <code>library/books/Moore-2020_Teaching-the-Empire_Habsburg-Schooling-and-State-Loyalty.pdf</code> — the <b>general</b> ladder (§1). Page references are printed book pages (add 11 for the PDF page).</li>\n<li><b>Lassnigg, Lorenz (2015).</b> <i>'Muddling through' and historical institutionalism — Explanatory devices for the long term development of the dualistic Austrian VET system.</i> IHS Sociological Series Working Paper 108, Institut für Höhere Studien, Vienna. <code>library/literature/Lassnigg-2015_Muddling-Through_Austrian-VET-System.pdf</code> — the <b>vocational</b> branch (§2). Page references are printed pages (add 10 for the PDF page).</li>\n<li><b>k.k. Statistische Zentralkommission (1912).</b> <i>Statistik der Unterrichtsanstalten in den im Reichsrate vertretenen Königreichen und Ländern für das Jahr 1908/1909</i> (<i>Österreichische Statistik</i>, XCIII. Band, 1. Heft). Wien: k.k. Hof- und Staatsdruckerei. <code>library/education/OeStat-1912_Bd-XCIII-1_Statistik-der-Unterrichtsanstalten-1908-09.pdf</code> — the administration's <b>own</b> taxonomy and counts (§2a). Roman folios are the <i>Einleitung</i>, arabic the tables; <code>reference/education/unterricht_page_index.csv</code> maps both to PDF pages.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</details>\n\n<p>Moore is a study of civic education, not of school administration. But chapter 1 (\"The Development of Education and\nCivic Education in Austria\", pp. 17–49) sets out the structure of the Cisleithanian system in the exact terms our field\nuses: which school, entered from where, for how many years, at what ages. That is what the <code>Vzdělání</code> strings encode.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"education-1-the-ladder-1869-1918\">1. The ladder, 1869–1918</h2>\n<p>Everything below is the settlement reached by the <strong>Reichsvolksschulgesetz</strong> of 14 May 1869 and still standing in 1914:\nthe law under which every man in our sample was schooled (birth cohorts ≈ 1875–1900).</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rung</th>\n<th>German</th>\n<th>Czech (as abbreviated in <code>Vzdělání</code>)</th>\n<th>Entered from</th>\n<th>Length</th>\n<th>Ages</th>\n<th>Moore</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Compulsory elementary</td>\n<td><strong>Volksschule</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-ob-cs\" data-gl=\"ob.\"><code>ob.</code></a> — obecná škola</td>\n<td>age 6</td>\n<td>5–8 yrs</td>\n<td>6–14</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compulsory upper elementary</td>\n<td><strong>Bürgerschule</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-mě-cs\" data-gl=\"mě.\"><code>mě.</code></a> — měšťanská škola</td>\n<td>after 5 yrs Volksschule</td>\n<td>3 yrs</td>\n<td>11–14</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Academic secondary</td>\n<td><strong>Gymnasium</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-gym-cs\" data-gl=\"gym.\"><code>gym.</code></a></td>\n<td>age 10 (from Volksschule)</td>\n<td>8 yrs</td>\n<td>10–18</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Technical secondary</td>\n<td><strong>Realschule</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-reálka-cs\" data-gl=\"reálka\"><code>reálka</code></a></td>\n<td>age 10</td>\n<td>7 yrs</td>\n<td>10–17</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid secondary</td>\n<td><strong>Real-Gymnasium</strong></td>\n<td>(rare)</td>\n<td>age 10</td>\n<td>8 yrs</td>\n<td>10–18</td>\n<td>30–31</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Girls' secondary</td>\n<td><strong>Lyzeum</strong></td>\n<td>(absent — male sample)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>31</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Teacher training</td>\n<td><strong>Lehrerbildungsanstalt</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-uč-ústav-cs\" data-gl=\"uč.ústav\"><code>uč.ústav</code></a>, <code>učitelský ústav</code></td>\n<td><strong>after Bürgerschule, age 15</strong></td>\n<td>4 yrs</td>\n<td>15–19</td>\n<td>29, 31, 184</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tertiary</td>\n<td><strong>Universität / Technische Hochschule</strong></td>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-univerzita-cs\" data-gl=\"univerzita\"><code>univerzita</code></a>, <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-technika-cs\" data-gl=\"technika\"><code>technika</code></a></td>\n<td>Gymnasium/Realschule <em>Matura</em></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>18+</td>\n<td>30, 24</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Four things in that table matter for the coding, and all four are counter-intuitive:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>The eight compulsory years are <code>ob. 5</code> + <code>mě. 3</code>.</strong> The 1869 law added two years to the Theresian six and set\n   compulsory attendance at ages 6–14; \"students could achieve this by attending Volksschule for five years followed by\n   an additional three years at a Bürgerschule\" (p. 30). So the most common structured string in our data, <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code>\n   (983 records, plus every spacing <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-variant-en\" data-gl=\"variant\">variant</a>), is <strong>the legal minimum, not an achievement</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Equally, <code>ob. 8</code> (2,813) is the <em>same</em> eight years taken entirely in a Volksschule with an upper stage. <code>ob. 8</code> and\n   <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code> are equal in years and unequal in curriculum; they must not be coded as if the second were a full rung\n   above the first.\n2. <strong>The Bürgerschule is not \"lower secondary\" in the modern sense.</strong> It is the compulsory upper elementary stage,\n   terminal by design: it \"provided additional general and vocational education to those students not planning to\n   attend university\" (p. 24, on the 1849 <em>Entwurf</em> that created it). It is a <em>branch</em> of the compulsory school, not a\n   step toward the Gymnasium.\n3. <strong>Gymnasium and Realschule are entered at age 10, in parallel with — not after — the Bürgerschule</strong> (p. 30). The\n   ladder forks at ten. A record showing <code>ob. 5 gym. 8</code> (72) or <code>ob. 5 reálka 7</code> (81) is a boy who left the compulsory\n   track at ten; <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code> is one who did not. This is a genuine ordinal break, and the one the field measures most\n   reliably.\n4. <strong>Teacher training sits on top of the Bürgerschule, not on top of a Matura.</strong> Teachers \"began their training after\n   completing Bürgerschule at the age of fifteen, receiving an additional four years of schooling at a teacher training\n   institution\" (p. 29). Austrian policy deliberately refused to <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-route-en\" data-gl=\"route\">route</a> them through Gymnasium and university (p. 29;\n   repeated p. 184), so <code>uč.ústav</code> (1,583 records) is <strong>not</strong> tertiary and not equivalent to a Realschule leaver: it is a\n   four-year vocational secondary qualification entered two rungs lower.</p>\n<h3 id=\"administration-and-why-the-ladder-is-uniform-enough-to-code\">Administration, and why the ladder is uniform enough to code</h3>\n<p>The May Laws kept a federalised system: crownland → district → local school board, with the ministry controlling only\n\"the universities, Gymnasien, Realschulen, and other secondary schools\" and Volksschule/Bürgerschule matters left\nentirely to the provincial boards (p. 31).</p>\n<p>Despite that, Moore finds the elementary curriculum \"remarkably similar throughout Austria\" from the 1870s to the 1910s\n(p. 32), and the ministry's policies \"applied to all public schools, regardless of its language of instruction\" (p. 32).\nSo the Czech-language schools our legionnaires attended ran on the same ladder as the German ones. <strong>That is the licence\nto treat <code>ob.</code>/<code>mě.</code> as one national scale.</strong></p>\n<h3 id=\"the-variation-moore-says-is-real-and-that-we-can-measure\">The variation Moore says is real, and that we can measure</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Urban vs rural is the binding constraint — not province, gender or language</strong> (p. 33). School hours were set by\n  school <em>size</em>: a one- or two-room rural school taught lower and upper grades in shifts, and after the conservative turn\n  of the 1880s–90s provincial boards let rural schools drop to <strong>half-day attendance</strong> — in Upper Austria, 98 of 124\n  one-room schools by 1913 (p. 34).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Two men both recorded <code>ob. 8</code> did not receive the same schooling, and the difference runs along the urban/rural axis\n  we already carry at <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-okres-cs\" data-gl=\"okres\">okres</a> level. An argument for using <code>birth_okres</code> covariates <em>alongside</em> the education ordinal, not\n  for abandoning the ordinal.\n- <strong>Eight years was politically contested throughout</strong> (pp. 34–35): <em>Das Vaterland</em> argued six years sufficed and that\n  more schooling made <em>worse</em> recruits — \"additional years in school would actually harm the quality of recruits,\n  because they would become too inquisitive and prone to question authority\". Useful framing for the paper —\n  contemporaries themselves theorised schooling → obedience — but not a coding input.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"education-2-the-vocational-branch-which-moore-does-not-reach\">2. The vocational branch, which Moore does not reach</h2>\n<p><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"lassnigg_2015\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Lassnigg (2015, above)</a> is an institutional history of Austrian vocational education written to explain the present-day\nsystem, so most of it is about the Republic. Its historical section (pp. 11–16) covers exactly the ~17 % of our field\nthat Moore leaves dark, and it settles the <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-pok-cs\" data-gl=\"pok.\"><code>pok.</code></a> question.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-pok-question-is-settled-the-fortbildungsschule-is-compulsory-schooling-not-secondary\">The <code>pok.</code> question is settled: the Fortbildungsschule is compulsory schooling, not secondary</h3>\n<p>Three findings, each independently decisive:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>It was legally part of compulsory mass schooling.</strong> Lassnigg names as a critical juncture \"the very early\n   decisions to treat the accompanying part-time school as part of compulsory (general mass) schooling, and consequently\n   to enclose these institutions into the decentralised local governance structures of compulsory schooling, whereas the\n   fulltime schools were developed from the central level\" (p. 18). The Fortbildungsschule sat in the <em>same</em> communal\n   governance box as the Volksschule and Bürgerschule — not with the Realschule and Gymnasium, which Moore (p. 31) puts\n   under the ministry.</li>\n<li><strong>It selected on nothing.</strong> \"Access to an enterprise based apprenticeship only depends on the decision of the\n   training enterprise, without being based on formal educational credentials; as a second step the obligation to\n   attend Berufsschule takes effect after an apprenticeship contract is concluded\" (p. 14). By contrast, the full-time\n   VET schools required \"academic lower secondary or good grades at Bürgerschule/Hauptschule, plus entrance exams\"\n   (p. 15). So <code>pok.</code> in a record carries <strong>no information about prior school performance</strong>; <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-obch-cs\" data-gl=\"obch.\"><code>obch.</code></a>, <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-prům-cs\" data-gl=\"prům.\"><code>prům.</code></a> and <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-odb-cs\" data-gl=\"odb.\"><code>odb.</code></a>\n   do.</li>\n<li><strong>Its ancestry is popular, not academic.</strong> The predecessors \"were originally rather related to popular mass\n   education (Sunday and evening schools)\" (p. 11) — Hankiewicz's genealogy runs Christenlehre → Wiederholungsschule →\n   Sonntagschule → Zeichenschule → … → Fortbildungsschule (p. 11 n. 5). Apprenticeship itself descends from the guilds\n   and was regulated by the <em>Gewerbeordnung</em>, i.e. <strong>trade law, not education law</strong> (p. 11).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>That places <code>pok.</code> (8,805 records) squarely inside the compulsory-plus tier, next to <code>mě.</code>; the first parser had it seven\nrungs too high (§4). It also explains <code>pok.</code> vs <code>pok.prům.</code>: two categories evolved, \"general (across a number of\ntrades: allgemein-gewerbliche Fortbildungsschulen) and specialised (for a certain trade), depending on the local numbers\nof apprentices (except in cities the former dominated quantitatively)\" (p. 13).</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-rest-of-the-branch\">The rest of the branch</h3>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Token</th>\n<th>Institution</th>\n<th>What Lassnigg establishes</th>\n<th>p.</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>prům.</code>, <code>vyšší prům.</code></td>\n<td><strong>Staatsgewerbeschule</strong></td>\n<td>Full-time, central jurisdiction, created by the <strong>Dumreicher plan from the 1880s</strong> as \"a network of trade and engineering schools across the monarchy\"; the higher tier linked upward to the Polytechnic/Technische Hochschule. A genuine secondary institution — and a <em>different</em> thing from <code>pok.prům.</code></td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>obch.</code></td>\n<td><strong>Handelsschule</strong></td>\n<td>Medium level, mostly <strong>private</strong>, \"much more stand-alone medium level schools than higher level colleges existed\"</td>\n<td>13, 15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>obch.ak.</code></td>\n<td><strong>Handelsakademie</strong></td>\n<td>Higher level college; the private commercial schools \"tried to acquire state recognition for their certificates\"; the Matura exam here was <strong>voluntary</strong></td>\n<td>13, 15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>odb.</code>, <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-hosp-cs\" data-gl=\"hosp.\"><code>hosp.</code></a></td>\n<td><strong>Fachschulen</strong> (trade, commerce, agriculture, home economics)</td>\n<td>Four sectoral traditions grew \"at local level in close relation to the economic activities\", with workshops at the core; agriculture stayed outside the education ministry entirely</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>reálka</code></td>\n<td><strong>Realschule (1805)</strong></td>\n<td>Originally the <em>vocationally oriented</em> alternative; became fully academic only in stages (1848, 1869, 1927, 1962). In our period it is explicitly \"a mediating mechanism between VET schools and higher education\"</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mě.</code></td>\n<td><strong>Bürgerschule (1869)</strong></td>\n<td>\"Established at the three upper grades (6–8) of primary school <strong>for purposes of commerce and administration</strong>\" — sharpens Moore's terminal-branch reading with a purpose</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"two-things-that-bear-directly-on-interpretation\">Two things that bear directly on interpretation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The full-time/apprentice split is partly a liquidity split, not an ability split.</strong> Full-time VET schools \"provided\n  the same credentials as an apprenticeship, however, whereas apprentices received a wage, attention to fulltime schools\n  had to be paid for\" (p. 15). A man with <code>prům.</code> or <code>obch.</code> rather than <code>pok.</code> differs from an apprentice in family\n  resources as well as in schooling. This is a caveat the paper should state wherever the education variable is read as\n  human capital; §2a puts a number on it.</li>\n<li><strong>Regulation was regional in our period.</strong> The Fortbildungsschule was governed at <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-land-de\" data-gl=\"land\">Land</a> and communal level, with the\n  regional laws set \"between 1907 and 1931\" (p. 13) and the apprenticeship/full-time separation not completed until\n  1925 (p. 13). So for the 1875–1900 birth cohorts the vocational branch was genuinely heterogeneous across crownlands,\n  in a way the compulsory ladder (§1) was not. Cross-okres comparisons of <code>pok.</code> are weaker than cross-okres comparisons\n  of <code>ob.</code>/<code>mě.</code></li>\n</ul>\n<details id=\"what-lassnigg-cannot-give-us\"><summary>What Lassnigg cannot give us</summary>\n\n<p>His quantitative series (Table 1) starts in <b>1924</b> and covers the Republic of Austria, not the Bohemian lands — so it is background, not a benchmark. It is still worth one line in the paper: his generational reconstruction (Table 2) puts the cohorts born <b>1865–1888</b> and <b>1883–1923</b> in upper secondary education in 1880–1907 and 1898–1942 respectively, which brackets our sample, and the first observation (1924) finds <b>82 % of 14–18-year-olds not in education at all</b>, with apprenticeship at 11 % against 2 % each for medium VET, higher VET and the academic track. Even allowing for territory and date, that is the order of magnitude: post-compulsory schooling of any kind was rare, and our <code>gym.</code>/<code>reálka</code>/<code>univerzita</code> records are a thin, selected top.</p>\n\n<p>He is silent on Hungary, and on the Czech lands specifically.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"education-2a-the-administration-s-own-taxonomy-1908-09\">2a. The administration's own taxonomy (1908/09)</h2>\n<p>Everything above §2 is secondary literature. Moore describes the law; Lassnigg's quantitative series begins in\n<strong>1924</strong>, in the Republic of Austria, on territory this sample does not cover. §5 of the first version of this document\nsaid as much, and named the filler: \"the Austrian statistical administration's own school taxonomy … which <em>classifies</em>\nschools rather than describing them.\"</p>\n<p>That source is now in hand — <em>Österreichische Statistik</em> XCIII/1 — and it was read against the ladder on 2026-09-07. The\nfull results are in <a href=\"#validation-education\"><code>VALIDATION_EDUCATION.md</code></a>; what bears on the ladder itself follows.</p>\n<p><strong>The state files the continuation school apart, in both branches.</strong> p. XX divides the vocational branch into <em>a)</em>\nFachschulen für gewerbliche Hauptgruppen, <em>b)</em> Fachschulen für einzelne gewerbliche Zweige, <em>c)</em> Handwerkerschulen and\n<em>d)</em> <strong>gewerbliche Fortbildungs- und Zeichenschulen</strong>. p. XVI divides the commercial one into 24 höhere Handelsschulen,\n115 kommerzielle <em>Tagesschulen</em> and <strong>168 kaufmännische Fortbildungsschulen</strong>.</p>\n<p>And in both it is the mass institution. Böhmen has <strong>504</strong> gewerbliche Fortbildungsschulen with <strong>50,836</strong> pupils,\nagainst 9 Staatsgewerbeschulen with 3,518 and 85 Fachschulen with 4,970 — <strong>84.0 %</strong> of all vocational pupils in the\nLand. §2's reading of <code>pok.</code> is the administration's own; the v1.0.0 reading would have put the largest and least\nselective school kind in the empire level with the Gymnasium.</p>\n<p><strong>The Bürgerschule was a selective step, not the ordinary sequel to the Volksschule.</strong> Table 34 counts <strong>1,266</strong>\nBürgerschulen against 20,975 allgemeine Volksschulen — <strong>5.7 %</strong> of public elementary institutions. In Böhmen 608, of\nwhich <strong>374 čecho-slavisch</strong> and 234 deutsch. Rung 2 has to be read at that rate.</p>\n<p><strong>⚠ The eight-year standard behind <code>education_complete</code> does not describe a school that existed.</strong> Table 34 also counts\nallgemeine Volksschulen by <strong>number of ascending classes</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>classes</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">1</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">2</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">3</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">4</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">5</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">6</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">7</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>8</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cisleithania</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,940</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,433</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,372</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,914</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,624</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">620</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">62</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>10</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Böhmen</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,112</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,703</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">951</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">562</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,114</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">97</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Ten eight-class Volksschulen in all of Cisleithania; two in the Czech lands; 1,114 five-class schools in Böhmen alone.\nMoore's eight years (p. 30) are a <strong>legal obligation spanning institutions</strong> — Volksschule 5 + Bürgerschule 3 — and\nTable 34's classes are an <strong>institutional form</strong>. <code>Vzdělání</code>'s bare <code>ob. N</code> does not say which of the two it records.\nThis was logged as <strong><a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a></strong> and is ruled on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>): 8 or more is complete, a number below 8 is <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code>; see §5.</p>\n<p><strong>The liquidity caveat has a number.</strong> At the Staatsgewerbeschulen (p. XXII), <strong>65.0 %</strong> of pupils were wholly exempt\nfrom Schulgeld and 1.2 % half. So §2's \"full-time VET had to be paid for\" is true of the fee schedule but not of most\npupils' families, and the ability/liquidity distinction is weaker than the fee alone suggests.</p>\n<p><strong>Parallel entry, in the source.</strong> p. VIII tabulates the <em>Vorstudien der Geprüften</em> for Gymnasium entrants as\n<strong>allgemeine Volks- oder Bürgerschulen</strong> against <em>Privatunterricht</em> — Böhmen 3,191 of 3,223. §1's age-ten fork, from the\nadministration rather than from Moore.</p>\n<p><strong>Two things the volume adds that the ladder had no place for.</strong> The <em>Notschule</em> (emergency one-teacher school, 379 in\nCisleithania) and the <em>Handwerkerschule</em> (13 in the empire). Neither is tokenised; neither matters for this sample — 1\nNotschule in the Czech lands against 277 in Tirol — but a study of Alpine births would need the first.</p>\n<p>⚠ <strong>The volume is Cisleithanian by definition</strong> (<em>\"in den im Reichsrate vertretenen Königreichen und Ländern\"</em>), so none\nof the above reaches Hungary, and <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> stays open for exactly the reason it already was.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"education-3-what-the-field-contains\">3. What the field contains</h2>\n<p><code>Vzdělání</code> is non-empty on <strong>105,992 of 132,993</strong> csol records (79.7 %), across 10,060 distinct strings. It is not a\nlevel: it is an <strong>itinerary</strong>, a sequence of school types, each optionally followed by the number of years completed\n(<code>ob. 5 mě. 3 pok. 3</code>). Eighteen token families reach <strong>98.9 %</strong> of the non-empty strings:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Token family</th>\n<th>Institution</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Records</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">% of non-empty</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ob.</code> / <code>ob 5</code> / <code>8 ob.</code></td>\n<td>Volksschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">77,275</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">72.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mě.</code> / <code>3mě</code></td>\n<td>Bürgerschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">23,517</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">22.2 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pok.</code> <code>pokr.</code> <code>pokrač.</code> <code>pok.prům.</code></td>\n<td><strong>Fortbildungsschule</strong> (see §2)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8,805</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8.3 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>obch.</code> <code>obch.šk.</code> <code>obchodní škola</code></td>\n<td>Handelsschule (2 yrs)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4,141</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>reálka</code></td>\n<td>Realschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4,138</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>prům.</code> <code>průmyslovka</code> <code>vyšší prům.</code></td>\n<td>Staatsgewerbeschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,853</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.6 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>gym.</code></td>\n<td>Gymnasium</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,540</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.3 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>odb.</code></td>\n<td>Fachschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,281</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2.2 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hosp.</code> <code>hosp.šk.</code></td>\n<td>landwirtschaftliche Schule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,676</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.6 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>uč.ústav</code></td>\n<td>Lehrerbildungsanstalt</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,583</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.5 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>univerzita</code> (+ <code>práva</code>, <code>medicína</code>…)</td>\n<td>Universität</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,493</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.4 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>obch.ak.</code> <code>obchodní akademie</code></td>\n<td>Handelsakademie (4 yrs, Matura)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,348</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.3 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>technika</code></td>\n<td>Technische Hochschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,033</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.0 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>analfabet</code></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">445</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.4 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>kadetka</code>, vojenská</td>\n<td>Kadettenschule</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">256</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.2 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>konzervatoř</code>, umělecká</td>\n<td>conservatory / art academy</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">92</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.1 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>?</code> <code>-</code></td>\n<td>placeholder</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">190</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.2 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bohoslovecká, seminář</td>\n<td>seminary</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">10</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.0 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>unmatched</em></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,135</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.1 %</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Families overlap — a string names several schools — so the column sums past 100 %. The counts are of the raw\n<code>Vzdělání</code> strings, which <code>data/final</code> does not carry, so they are typed here rather than read from the build. The unmatched tail is mostly\nspelled-out or truncated variants of the same institutions (<code>učit.ústav</code>, <code>práv.fak.</code>, <code>lesnická škola</code>, <code>střední\nškola</code>, <code>umprum</code>, <code>selské učiliště</code>): a dictionary problem, not a new rung.</p>\n<p><strong>The year counts are usable.</strong> Because the law fixes the length of every rung, a count that falls short of it is\ninformative: <code>ob. 3</code> (1,212) or <code>ob. 2</code> (703) is an interrupted compulsory education, and under the half-day regime\nabove it plausibly means very little schooling at all. A count that meets it (<code>ob. 5</code>, <code>mě. 3</code>, <code>reálka 7</code>, <code>gym. 8</code>)\nmeans completion.</p>\n<p>A truncated secondary count (<code>gym. 4</code>, <code>reálka 4</code>) means the <strong>lower</strong> Gymnasium/Realschule without Matura: a real and\nrecognised exit point in the Austrian system, not a parsing artefact.</p>\n<h2 id=\"education-4-what-the-first-parser-got-wrong-v1-0-0\">4. What the first parser got wrong (v1.0.0)</h2>\n<p><code>utils/parsing/education.py</code> v1.0.0 collapsed everything into a five-level ordinal by first-match substring rules.\nAgainst the ladder above it had four defects, and §6 is what replaced it:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>pok.</code> was scored <em>Upper secondary</em>, level with <code>gym.</code>, though it is not secondary at all;</li>\n<li>dot-less and long variants (<code>pokr.</code>, <code>3mě</code>) fell through, and several schools had no rule;</li>\n<li><code>uč.ústav</code> was coded level with <code>gym.</code>/<code>reálka</code>, though it is entered from the Bürgerschule at fifteen;</li>\n<li>the first match won on a string that describes a whole career.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This is the same failure shape logged elsewhere in the project: an unanchored substring rule that is narrower than its\nsource (cf. <code>ranks</code> 1.4.0, <code>occupations</code> 1.1.0). The four defects as this section first described them, with their\ncounts, are under <em>How we got here</em>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"education-5-what-is-still-open\">5. What is still open</h2>\n<p>The taxonomy is closed (§2a). What stays open is the completion flag, the Hungarian half, and three things no source here\ncan give: the vocational branch's duration, how completely <code>pok.</code> was written down, and attendance.</p>\n<h3 id=\"open-for-the-author\">Open for the author</h3>\n<p>Until the author rules, each stays as its <em>Default now</em> cell says.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Ruling</th>\n<th>Default now</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n<th>Where</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>A bare <code>ob. N</code>: years attended or classes completed?</strong> Ruled on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>), a third way beside the two that stood here: 8 means finished, anything below 8 is unknown.</td>\n<td><code>education.py</code> 2.2.0: <code>education_complete</code> is True at 8 or more and <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code> below 8; the stated number is kept and is not years of schooling</td>\n<td>Czech-lands births: 3,899 scored complete, 0 <code>ob. 5</code> scored incomplete (none since 2.2.0)</td>\n<td><a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>; the checks, Check 3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>The Hungarian ladder</strong>: score each frame against its own law (with <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a>), and interact the ordinal with a Cisleithanian/Transleithanian indicator. Ruled for the completion flag on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-277\">D-277</a>): six elementary years are the full course for a birth in the Hungarian part (<code>education.add_frame_completion</code>, 2.3.0). The validation of the Hungarian rungs still waits on a source.</td>\n<td>one ordinal across both frames; Slovak births held to the Austrian completion length</td>\n<td>0 Slovak births with the full six-year course scored <code>education_complete = False</code></td>\n<td><a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a>; below</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><code>ob. 8</code> against <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code>: which is the higher signal?</strong> Ruled on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-276\">D-276</a>): the ladder is kept. The two are the same in years and both finished (<code>education_complete</code>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>); they differ in which school was reached, which is what <code>education_ord</code> records. Internal evidence (rank at entry, occupation, <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-hisclass-en\" data-gl=\"hisclass\">HISCLASS</a>) puts the burgher-school men higher, also among men born in the same municipality</td>\n<td>the ladder puts the Bürgerschule a rung above the Volksschule</td>\n<td>every <code>ob. 8</code> and every <code>mě.</code> record</td>\n<td>below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Waiting on a source, not a ruling:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>the vocational branch's duration</strong>: no source here gives the Fortbildungsschule's weekly hours or the Fachschulen's\n  course lengths, so <code>education_complete</code> stays <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code> across that branch and no <code>education_years_total</code> is emitted;</li>\n<li><strong>attendance against enrolment</strong>: Table 39 of the 1908/09 volume defines the reduced-attendance schools and counts them\n  by Land, not by Bezirk, so there is still no okres covariate;</li>\n<li><strong>the Hungarian sources</strong>, located 2026-11-03: the 1868 law is read (below); Kornis 1932 is in <code>library/education/</code>\n  (not yet read on 2026-11-03); the 1910 Hungarian census and Puttkamer 2003 are named.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>A caveat that stays: <code>pok.</code> is under-recorded.</strong> The Czech lands had about six times more continuation pupils per\nfull-time vocational pupil in 1908/09 than the records name. <code>education_apprentice</code> (6.6 %\nof records) is therefore a <strong>lower bound on apprenticeship, not a rate</strong>, and must not be read as the share of the\ncohort that served one.</p>\n<p><strong>Open work:</strong> the hand-coded check of the tokeniser is drawn and not yet coded (the checks, Check 6); notebook 03's\neducation figures were composed for five rungs, and whether their palette and stacking still want an eye after its\nre-run has not been looked at.</p>\n<details><summary>The open items in full, as revised 2026-09-07 and 2026-11-03</summary>\n\n<p><i>Revised 2026-09-07, after the external check in §2a. Three of the four items below moved; one did not, and one is new.</i></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>The vocational branch — the taxonomy is closed, the duration is not.</b> §2a settles <i>where</i> the administration itself put each vocational institution, which is what the ordinal needed and what §5 previously asked this class of source for. What the 1908/09 volume still does <b>not</b> give is <b>duration</b>: it classifies and counts schools without stating the Fortbildungsschule's weekly hours or the Fachschulen's course lengths, which varied by Land and by trade (regional laws 1907–1931). So <code>pok. 3</code> and <code>odb. 2</code> remain years of a thing whose size we do not know, <code>education_complete</code> stays <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code> across that branch, and no <code>education_years_total</code> is emitted.</li>\n\n<li><b>Hungary. Unchanged, and now the only reason <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> is open.</b> Moore is explicit that his account \"only appl[ies] to Austrian schools and not those in Hungary\", the Ausgleich having handed Hungarian schools to Budapest (p. 36). Lassnigg is silent on Hungary too, and the 1908/09 volume is <i>\"in den im Reichsrate vertretenen Königreichen und Ländern\"</i> — Cisleithania <b>by definition</b>, so it cannot help either. The ~10,500 Slovakia-born records are excluded from every test in <a href=\"#validation-education\">VALIDATION_EDUCATION.md</a>. Slovak and Rusyn legionnaires were schooled under a different law (Eötvös 1868, then the Apponyi laws of 1907), with a different ladder and a Magyarising language policy. <b>One ordinal cannot silently span both frames</b>; at minimum this wants a Cisleithanian/Transleithanian indicator interacted with the level, the way <code>birth_okres</code> and <code>birth_jaras_id</code> are already kept apart. The fix is a Hungarian source, not another pass over the strings.\n\n<p><b>Sources located 2026-11-03.</b> (1) The law itself, Act XXXVIII of 1868 on public elementary education, in full on <i>Ezer év törvényei</i> (net.jogtar.hu, docid 86800038.TV; its robots.txt bars AI agents, so the text is not in <code>library/</code> — save it by hand). As read there: school is compulsory from 6 to 12, or to 15 (§ 1). The everyday elementary school runs <b>6</b> years, against Bohemia's 5, and is followed by up to 3 years of a part-time <i>ismétlő iskola</i> (repetition school), 5 hours a week in winter and 2 in summer (§§ 48–52), which is the nearest Hungarian counterpart of the <code>pok.</code> continuation school. The <i>felső népiskola</i> (upper elementary school) is entered after the six classes and runs 3 years for boys (§§ 61–62). The <i>polgári iskola</i> (burgher school) is entered after the <b>fourth</b> class, not the fifth, and runs 6 years for boys and 4 for girls (§§ 68–69). Act XXX of 1883 governs the 8-class gymnasium and real school. (2) An English overview, Kornis, <i>Education in Hungary</i> (Teachers College, Columbia, 1932), free on the Hungarian Academy's REAL-EOD (record 8622); in <code>library/education/</code> since 2026-11-03, not yet read. (3) The state's own figures, the counterpart of §2a: the 1910 Hungarian census, the first to ask completed schooling (secondary classes completed), by county and town; its volumes are in the KSH collection on Hungaricana (<i>Magyar Statisztikai Közlemények</i>, n.s. 64 per Karády 2025). (4) The Slovak side, Puttkamer, <i>Schulalltag und nationale Integration in Ungarn</i> (Oldenbourg, 2003), on Slovak and Romanian schooling under the Hungarian state idea, 1867–1914.</p>\n\n<p><b>The records already follow the law</b> (build of 2026-09-23). Of Slovak births whose top rung is the elementary school, 56.2 % state <b>6</b> years, against 26.2 % at 5 and 32.5 % at 8 for Czech-lands births. A Slovak burgher school runs to 4 years (34 % of those stating years), a Czech one to 3 (62 %). So the rungs carry over, and the years at each are the Hungarian law's. What does not carry over is the completion standard: <b>789</b> Slovak records with the full six-year everyday course are scored <code>education_complete = False</code>, held to the Austrian length. The fix belongs with <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a> below: each frame scored against its own law.</p></li>\n\n<li><b>⚠ Whether a bare <code>ob. N</code> counts years or classes. Newly opened, and it breaks a column.</b> §2a's Table 34 shows the eight-class Volksschule <code>education_complete</code> scores against existed <b>10 times in Cisleithania and twice in the Czech lands</b>. Among 11,986 Czech-lands-born records with <code>education_top == \"elementary\"</code> and a stated year, <b>3,894</b> are scored complete against that form and <b>3,137</b> reading <code>ob. 5</code> — the modal <i>full</i> Bohemian Volksschule — are scored incomplete. Logged as <b><a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a></b> with two candidate resolutions: (a) set <code>education_complete</code> to <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code> for a bare <code>ob. N</code>, refusing to judge as the vocational branch already does, or (b) re-base the standard on 5. (a) is recommended; (b) resolves by assumption exactly where the source shows the ambiguity is real. <b>Not yet applied</b> — it changes an emitted column.</li>\n\n<li><b>⚠ How completely <code>pok.</code> is recorded at all. New.</b> The Czech lands had <b>5.3</b> continuation pupils per full-time vocational pupil in 1908/09; the records name them at <b>0.86</b> to one, about <b>6× fewer</b>. The continuation school was compulsory, part-time and unremarkable, and men appear simply not to have written it down. <code>education_apprentice</code> (6.6 %) is a <b>lower bound on apprenticeship, not a rate</b>, and must not be read as the share of the cohort that served one. Flow-vs-stock and selection into the Legion also contribute, and nothing available can apportion the three.</li>\n\n<li><b>Whether <code>ob. 8</code> ≡ <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code>. Narrowed.</b> Moore gives us that they are equal in <i>years</i> (p. 30) and differ in <i>curriculum</i> (p. 30: the Bürgerschule added practical agricultural and industrial subjects). §2a adds that they were nothing like equally common — the Bürgerschule was <b>5.7 %</b> of public elementary institutions, and the state examined its teachers separately (4,618 Volksschule against 865 Bürgerschule Lehrbefähigungsprüfungen, p. XVI). So <code>mě.</code> marks a selective step and not the ordinary sequel. Which is the higher <i>signal</i> is still an assumption to be stated, not a fact any of the three sources supplies; internal evidence — rank at entry, occupation, HISCLASS — can adjudicate it the way <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-33\">D-33</a> adjudicated <code>rolník</code>.</li>\n\n<li><b>Attendance vs enrolment. Narrowed, not closed.</b> The half-day rural regime (Moore p. 34) means recorded years overstate contact hours, unevenly and in a direction correlated with rurality. Table 39 of the 1908/09 volume defines the thing exactly — schools where \"die Kinder ganzer Ortschaften oder Weiler die Schule <b>wöchentlich nur ein bis dreimal</b> besuchen\" — and counts them, but <b>by Land, not by Bezirk</b>. So there is now an administrative definition and a crownland magnitude, and still no okres covariate and nothing at the individual level.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</details>\n\n<h2 id=\"education-6-the-revision-as-implemented-education-py-2-0-0-extended-in-2-1-0\">6. The revision, as implemented (<code>education.py</code> 2.0.0, extended in 2.1.0)</h2>\n<p><strong>Parse, don't classify.</strong> The module tokenises the itinerary — institution names and the numbers attached to them —\nand reports the <strong>highest institution attended</strong>, the years at each rung, and the track. Eleven columns, <code>educ_clean</code> /\n<code>educ_ord</code> keeping their old names so <code>schema.py</code> and notebook 03 keep working.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">ord</th>\n<th>Label</th>\n<th>Institutions on this rung</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0</td>\n<td>No schooling</td>\n<td><code>analfabet</code>; <code>žádné</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1</td>\n<td>Elementary</td>\n<td>Volksschule (<code>ob.</code>, <code>obecná</code>, <code>národní škola</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2</td>\n<td>Burgher school</td>\n<td>Bürgerschule (<code>mě.</code>, <code>měšťanská</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n<td>Vocational secondary</td>\n<td>Handelsschule (<code>obch.</code>) · Staatsgewerbeschule (<code>prům.</code>) · Fachschule (<code>odb.</code>, <code>lesnická</code>, <code>učiliště</code>) · landw. Schule (<code>hosp.</code>, <code>zemědělská</code>, <code>selská</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4</td>\n<td>Upper secondary</td>\n<td>Gymnasium (<code>gym.</code>) · Realschule (<code>reálka</code>) · Handelsakademie (<code>obch.ak.</code>) · higher Staatsgewerbeschule (<code>vyšší prům.</code>) · Lehrerbildungsanstalt (<code>uč.ústav</code>) · Kadettenschule (<code>kadetka</code>) · conservatory (<code>konzervatoř</code>, <code>umprum</code>) · <code>střední škola</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5</td>\n<td>Tertiary</td>\n<td>Universität (<code>univerzita</code>, <code>vš</code>, <code>fakulta</code>) · Technische Hochschule (<code>technika</code>) · theology (<code>bohoslovecká</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">—</td>\n<td><strong>off the ordinal</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fortbildungsschule</strong> (<code>pok.</code>, <code>pokr.</code>, <code>pokrač.</code>, <code>pok.prům.</code>) — carried by <code>educ_apprentice</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><code>ladder_report()</code> prints this table with the native names, tracks and standard course lengths.</p>\n<p><strong>The ladder in <code>data/final</code></strong> (the highest rung each record names, of all 132,993\nrecords):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code>education</code></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">records</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">share</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>No schooling</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">449</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.3 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Elementary</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">64,870</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">48.8 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Burgher school</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">19,883</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">15.0 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vocational secondary</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">7,900</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Upper secondary</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">9,146</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tertiary</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,792</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2.1 %</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>missing: empty or unparsed</em></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">27,953</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><code>education_apprentice</code> is true on 8,814 records (6.6 %).\n<strong>99.1 %</strong> of non-empty cells parse (measured on the raw field when 2.1.0 landed, §6a).</p>\n<p><strong>Design decisions worth naming</strong>, each traceable to §1 or §2:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Same years, different school.</strong> <code>ob. 8</code> and <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code> are both eight years of schooling, and both are\n  marked finished. The ordinal still puts the second a rung higher, because it records the school a man reached,\n  not how long he sat in one. Which road a man took depended mostly on whether a burgher school was within reach\n  of his birthplace; the men who took it stand higher in occupation and rank even among men born in the same\n  municipality (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-276\">D-276</a>). Whether the school or the family behind it made the difference is not known.</li>\n<li><strong>The ordinal is attendance, not attainment.</strong> A bare <code>reálka</code> does not say whether the man finished, so completion is\n  a separate column (<code>educ_complete</code>) that is allowed to be missing, rather than a guess folded into the level.\n  <code>educ_complete</code> is <code>pd.NA</code> for the whole vocational branch, because §5's residue is exactly that no source gives those\n  course lengths.</li>\n<li><strong><code>pok.</code> sets a floor of 1, never a rung.</strong> A continuation school followed the eight compulsory years, so a record\n  naming only <code>pok.</code> implies elementary schooling. It can raise a record from <em>unknown</em> to <em>Elementary</em>, and can never\n  raise it past what the string states.</li>\n<li><strong>The Volksschule standard is eight years.</strong> A record that also names a Bürgerschule has <code>burgher</code> as its top rung and\n  is scored against <em>its</em> standard of 3 (§6a). Whether a bare <code>ob. N</code> should be judged at all is <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a> (§5).</li>\n<li><strong><code>prům.</code> vs <code>vyšší prům.</code> splits on the qualifier</strong>, one rung apart, the same way <code>occupation_qualifier</code> splits\n  <code>zámečník</code> from <code>strojní zámečník</code> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-29\">D-29</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Years attach positionally</strong>, backwards to the institution they follow (<code>ob. 5</code>) and forwards when the string opens\n  with a number (<code>8 ob.</code>, <code>3mě</code>), so the dot-less variants that fell through v1.0.0 now parse.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"6a-what-210-added-d-51\">6a. What 2.1.0 added (D-51)</h3>\n<p>Three things the 2.0.0 rewrite left unresolved, all found by running the parser back over the raw field rather than by\nreading it.</p>\n<p><strong>The tie-break.</strong> Some records name two schools on the <em>same</em> rung — <code>reálka</code> + <code>obch. akademie</code>, <code>gym.</code> + <code>uč.ústav</code>,\n<code>odb.</code> + <code>hosp.</code> — and <code>max()</code> alone resolved them by insertion order, i.e. by which school the clerk happened to write\nfirst. The order is now written down in <code>education.TIE_BREAK</code>, on two principles:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A generic word yields to a specific one.</strong> <code>odb.</code> (<em>odborná</em> = \"specialised\") and <code>střední</code> (\"secondary\") are what\n   the source writes when it does <em>not</em> name the school — \"odborná hospodářská škola\" is one school, not two. <code>střední</code> is\n   dropped outright when the record names anything on rung 3 or above (83 records move; \"ob., střední\" with nothing else\n   post-compulsory still stands on its own).</li>\n<li><strong>The terminal professional school outranks the general school that feeds it.</strong> A man who wrote \"reálka, uč.ústav\"\n   finished as a teacher — §1 has the Lehrerbildungsanstalt entered <em>from</em> the Bürgerschule at fifteen, and it is where\n   his schooling ends. Same for the cadet school, the commercial academy and the conservatory.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Principle 2 rests on reading the cell as a chronological itinerary, which §3 argues from the field's structure and which\nthe data supports: on <strong>92.4 %</strong> of multi-rung records the ordinals never fall along the string.</p>\n<p><strong>Semesters are not years.</strong> <code>sem.</code>/<code>semestr</code> and its number are lifted out into <code>educ_semesters</code>\n(722 records) before the itinerary is scanned. Universities counted in semesters and the\nMittelschulen in years, and the two must not share a column.</p>\n<p><strong>The scan is word-anchored.</strong> Every institution pattern has to start at a word start. Without it <code>technik</code> matched\ninside <em>hydrotechnika</em> and <code>ob</code> inside <em>pob.</em> — the unanchored substring shape that <code>ranks</code> 1.4.0 had to remove after\nFidler caught <code>generálmajor</code> scoring as <code>major</code>. The number group is deliberately left unanchored so \"reálka4\" still\nyields 4.</p>\n<p><strong>A flagged floor.</strong> Where the only school named is the continuation school, the ordinal is floored at Elementary:\n1,112 records where <code>educ_top</code> names a school <code>educ_institutions</code> does not list. Those carry\n<code>educ_top_imputed = True</code> and the track <code>continuation</code> rather than <code>compulsory</code>, and the <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-qa-gate-en\" data-gl=\"qa gate\">QA gate</a> asserts that this is the\n<em>only</em> case where the two disagree.</p>\n<details><summary>What each 2.1.0 change moved, measured when it landed</summary>\n\n<p><b>The tie-break.</b> 1,512 records name two schools on the <i>same</i> rung. The same pair came out both ways: <code>obch.</code> + <code>odb.</code> gave <i>commercial</i> on 20 records and <i>trade</i> on 164. It is not cosmetic: it fixes <code>educ_track</code> (academic vs teacher vs military) and <code>educ_complete</code>, whose standard course lengths differ across the tied schools (Realschule 7, Lehrerbildungsanstalt 4).</p>\n\n<p><b>Semesters.</b> They used to attach backwards to the preceding institution and land in <code>educ_years_secondary</code>, so \"ob. 4 gym. 8 univerzita 8 sem.\" recorded eight <i>years</i> at the university.</p>\n\n<p><b>Anchoring.</b> Eight records stop parsing as a result, six of them correctly (<code>pob.</code>, <code>iob.</code>, <code>dělostř.š.</code>); the two <code>všeob.</code> records are a genuine loss and are left unparsed rather than guessed at. Anchoring the scan exposed three abbreviations the source uses and the patterns did not cover, now added: <code>univ.</code> (55 records, previously only <code>univer…</code>), <code>lék.fak.</code> / <code>fil.fak.</code> / <code>práv.fak.</code> (the faculty abbreviation, previously only the full <code>fakulta</code>), and <code>vyš.prům.</code> (37 records, previously only the full <code>vyšší</code>, so they fell to the 3-year Fachschule instead of the 4-year Staatsgewerbeschule). Coverage 99.07 % → <b>99.10 %</b> of non-empty cells.</p>\n\n<p><b>One dead branch removed.</b> <code>educ_complete</code> computed the Volksschule standard as \"5 if a Bürgerschule follows, else 8\". The five can never be reached: the Bürgerschule outranks the Volksschule, so a record naming both has <code>burgher</code> as its top rung and is scored against <i>its</i> standard of 3. Measured on the full field: 0 records. The Volksschule standard is simply 8.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<h2 id=\"education-citation\">Citation</h2>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"nc\">@book</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nl\">moore2020teaching</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">author</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Moore, Scott O.}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">title</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Teaching the Empire: Education and State Loyalty in Late Habsburg Austria}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">series</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Central European Studies}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">publisher</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Purdue University Press}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">address</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{West Lafayette, IN}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">year</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{2020}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nc\">@techreport</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nl\">lassnigg2015muddling</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">author</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Lassnigg, Lorenz}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">title</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{'Muddling through' and historical institutionalism -- Explanatory devices for the long term development of the dualistic Austrian VET system}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">institution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Institut f\\\"ur H\\\"ohere Studien (IHS)}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">type</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{IHS Sociological Series Working Paper}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">number</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{108}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">address</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Vienna}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">year</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{2015}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">url</span><span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{https://irihs.ihs.ac.at/id/eprint/3735/}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nc\">@book</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nl\">ost1912unterrichtsanstalten</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">author</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{{k.k. Statistische Zentralkommission}}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">title</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Statistik der Unterrichtsanstalten in den im Reichsrate vertretenen K\\\"onigreichen und L\\\"andern f\\\"ur das Jahr 1908/1909}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">series</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{\\\"Osterreichische Statistik}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">volume</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{XCIII. Band, 1. Heft}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">publisher</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{k.k. Hof- und Staatsdruckerei}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">address</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{Wien}</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"na\">year</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">{1912}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"education-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</h2>\n<details><summary>What changed on this page, and when</summary>\n\n<p><b>The page.</b> In the docs pass (2026-11-20) it became the top of <i>Education</i>; the ladder's counts in §6 are read from <code>data/final</code> at every build, and the dated passages below moved here word for word.</p>\n\n<p><b>The status box, as it stood before the docs pass.</b></p>\n\n<blockquote><p><b>Status.</b> <b>Built.</b> <code>utils/parsing/education.py</code> is <b>v2.1.0</b> (v2.0.0 rebuilt it on the two sources below; 2.1.0 added the tie-break, semesters and word anchoring, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-51\">D-51</a>); <code>schema.py</code> carries the columns; notebook 02 was last re-run <b>2026-09-23</b> and <code>data/final</code> is current, QA gate <b>107/107</b> — the first build to carry the 2.1.0 columns (<code>education_semesters</code>, <code>education_top_imputed</code>), which the 2026-09-03 build predated (audit 2026-09-22 A6). <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> stays <b>Open</b> — not because the code is unfinished, but because the ladder is established for <b>Cisleithania only</b> and the Hungarian half of the sample rides on it unvalidated (§5).</p></blockquote>\n\n<p><b>§1 and §2 against the first parser.</b> §1's fourth point ended: \"The current module has it in the same bucket as <code>gym.</code>\" §2 said Lassnigg \"settles the largest open question in §5 below\", and that <code>pok.</code> \"confirms it is currently promoted seven rungs too far\". Both described <code>education</code> 1.0.0. §2 also opened with the source in full: <b>Source.</b> Lassnigg, Lorenz (2015). <i>'Muddling through' and historical institutionalism — Explanatory devices for the long term development of the dualistic Austrian VET system.</i> IHS Sociological Series Working Paper 108, Institut für Höhere Studien, Vienna (now in the Sources list at the top).</p>\n\n<p><b>§4, as first written: \"What this catches in the current implementation\".</b> <code>utils/parsing/education.py</code> v1.0.0 collapses everything into a five-level ordinal by first-match substring rules. Against the ladder above, four defects:</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><b><code>pok.</code> is scored \"Upper secondary\" and is not secondary at all.</b> The <i>pokračovací (živnostenská) škola</i> — the gewerbliche <b>Fortbildungsschule</b> — is the compulsory part-time continuation school for apprentices, attended a few hours a week <i>alongside</i> a trade apprenticeship after the eight compulsory years. It is the bottom of the vocational branch, not a rung above the Bürgerschule. Because its rule fires before <code>mě.</code> and <code>ob.</code>, every <code>ob. 5 mě. 3 pok. 3</code> record — the classic apprentice itinerary — currently lands in the same bucket as <code>gym.</code> <b>8,805 records, 8.3% of the non-empty field.</b> This is the largest single error in the variable, and it confirms ROADMAP B3.</li>\n<li><b>Dot-less and long variants fall through.</b> <code>pokr.</code>, <code>pokrač.</code>, <code>3mě</code>, <code>2mě</code> do not contain the literal tokens <code>pok.</code> / <code>mě.</code>; <code>hosp.</code>, <code>odb.</code>, <code>kadetka</code>, <code>konzervatoř</code> have no rule at all, and the 1.1% unmatched tail returns <code>None</code> unless an <code>ob.</code> elsewhere in the string rescues it at Primary.</li>\n<li><b><code>uč.ústav</code> is coded level with <code>gym.</code>/<code>reálka</code>.</b> Per Moore p. 29 it is entered <i>from the Bürgerschule at fifteen</i>, runs four years, and is explicitly not an academic track. It belongs a rung lower, or on a separate vocational axis.</li>\n<li><b>First-match-wins on a string that describes a whole career.</b> <code>reálka technika</code> (99), <code>gym. univerzita</code> (44), <code>ob. 5 mě. 3 uč.ústav 4</code> (38) are itineraries; the rules read only the first token they happen to hit. The field supports <b>highest rung reached</b> <i>plus</i> <b>years at each rung</b>, and should be parsed that way rather than classified.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><b>The 2.0.0 design rule that 2.1.0 removed.</b> §6 listed among its design decisions: \"<b>The Volksschule standard is itinerary-dependent</b> — 8 years alone, 5 when a Bürgerschule follows (§1.1). <code>ob. 5</code> alone is therefore <i>incomplete</i>; <code>ob. 5 mě. 3</code> is complete.\" §6a's dead branch is that rule's second half.</p>\n\n<p><b>Result on the full csol frame</b> (132,993 records; not yet written to <code>data/final</code>), when 2.0.0 was written:</p>\n\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th></th><th>v1.0.0</th><th>v2.0.0</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Non-empty strings parsed</td><td>96.7 %</td><td><b>99.1 %</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Records the <code>pok.</code> rule put in the <code>gym.</code> bucket</td><td>8,117</td><td><b>0</b></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n\n<p>The v1.0.0 <i>Upper secondary</i> bucket (18,756) redistributes: 7,579 stay, <b>3,973</b> move to Vocational secondary, <b>2,606</b> to Burgher school, <b>4,598</b> to Elementary. Ladder after the rewrite: Elementary 64,876 (48.8 %), Burgher school 19,884 (15.0 %), Upper secondary 9,320 (7.0 %), Vocational secondary 7,845 (5.9 %), Tertiary 2,630 (2.0 %), No schooling 449 (0.3 %), unparsed/empty 27,989 (21.0 %). <code>educ_apprentice</code> is true on <b>8,815</b> records (6.6 %).</p>\n\n<p><b>Landed 2026-09-02.</b> Notebook 02 re-run, QA gate <b>66/66</b>, <code>data/final/persons/</code> and the data dictionary rebuilt with all eleven columns. One label changed between the first run and the second: rung 0 was called <code>None</code>, which in any <code>value_counts</code> is indistinguishable from a missing value — the same shape as the fabricated-<code>exit_N</code> bug the 2026-07-16 audit found. It is <b><code>No schooling</code></b> now, and in the built frame the two read apart cleanly: <code>No schooling</code> 449, missing 27,989.</p>\n\n<p><b>Still to do,</b> as §6 ended until the docs pass: \"notebook 03's education figures import <code>EDUC_ORDER</code> symbolically, so they will run against the six labels, but they were composed for five and the palette and stacking want an eye. Those figures have not been re-run since 2026-08-02.\" Notebook 03 has re-run since; whether the palette and stacking still want an eye is listed as open work in §5.</p>\n\n</details><h2 id=\"education-the-ladder-in-the-data\">The ladder in the data</h2><p class=\"note\">Built by <code>notebooks/03_visualisation.ipynb</code> from <code>data/final</code>. The stack is coloured on the sequential ramp, not the categorical palette, because the variable is ordinal: light at the bottom rung, navy at the top. Click to enlarge.</p><div class='figgrid'><figure><img src=\"images/8ef6d2e3b850023f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Educ by theatre\" onclick=\"zoom(this)\" title=\"Click to enlarge\"><figcaption><b class=\"figno\">Figure 1</b> — Educ by theatre<br><code>output/figures/descriptives/composition/educ_by_theatre.png</code></figcaption></figure></div></section><section class=\"part\" id=\"part-validation-education\" data-part=\"validation-education\"><h2 class=\"parth\">External validation — education</h2><p class=\"lede partlede\">The Austrian school statistics of 1908/09 on the education ladder. · source: <code>reference/VALIDATION_EDUCATION.md</code></p><div class=\"sheetroot\" id=\"sheet-validation-education\"><div class=\"tldr\"><div class=\"tldr-h\">In short</div><p>External checks on the school ladder <code>education.py</code> builds; the method they check is\n<a href=\"#education\"><code>EDUCATION_LADDER.md</code></a>. One external source, five tests,\n<code>utils/reference_tools/education/run_unterricht_check.py</code>, and a sixth check by hand. All of them are indexed, with\nwhat each one is blind to, in <a href=\"#validation-register\"><code>VALIDATION.md</code></a>.</p></div><details class=\"feyn\"><summary>Explain it simply</summary><div class=\"feyn-b\"><p>What a soldier wrote in the schooling box — <i>ob. 5 mě. 3</i> and the like — only means something if you know what those schools were. Until now that knowledge came from two modern history books. Neither counts schools; one of them starts its figures in 1924, in a different country.</p><p>This page checks the scheme against the thing itself: the Austrian government's own annual census of every school it ran, printed in Vienna in 1912 for the year 1908/09, with a table for each kind of school in each province and the language it taught in. It is the register the ladder should have been built on, and it says three things.</p><p>It <b>confirms</b> the awkward call at the heart of the variable. The <i>pokračovací</i> school — compulsory evening classes for apprentices — had been treated as a rung above the rest, which would have made an apprentice look better-educated than a grammar-school boy. The government filed it in a category of its own, and it was enormous: 504 of them in Bohemia teaching 50,836 pupils, against nine state trade schools teaching 3,518. Leaving it off the ladder was right.</p><p>It <b>breaks</b> something else. The code marks an elementary schooling “complete” at eight years, because the law required eight years of schooling. But the census counts schools by how many year-groups they actually had, and a <i>eight</i>-class elementary school existed ten times in the whole empire and twice in the Czech lands. Nearly four thousand men are recorded as having finished a school that was almost nowhere, and three thousand more who wrote down the ordinary full five years are marked as having dropped out. The column is being left alone until that is decided properly rather than patched.</p><p>And it shows that the evening classes are <b>badly under-recorded</b>: in life there were five of those pupils for every full-time trade-school pupil, but in these records there are fewer than one. Men simply did not write down the classes they were obliged to attend. So that flag counts some apprentices, not all of them.</p><p>What none of it touches is Hungary. The volume covers only the Austrian half of the monarchy, and about ten thousand men here were schooled in the Hungarian half under different laws. That gap is old, and it stays.</p></div></details><nav class=\"toc\"><span>On this page</span><a href=\"#validation-education-the-source\">The source</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-1-the-ladder-against-the-state-s-own-list-of-school-kinds-run-taxonomy\">Check 1 — the ladder against the state&#x27;s own list of school kinds (run_taxonomy)</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-2-is-pok-a-rung-or-a-separate-kind-of-thing-run-continuation\">Check 2 — is pok. a rung, or a separate kind of thing? (run_continuation)</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-3-table-34-against-education-complete-run-klassen-fails\">Check 3 — Table 34 against education_complete (run_klassen) ⚠ FAILS</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-4-continuation-full-time-vocational-run-composition\">Check 4 — continuation : full-time vocational (run_composition)</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-5-the-czech-language-benchmark-and-how-selective-rung-2-was-run-language\">Check 5 — the Czech-language benchmark, and how selective rung 2 was (run_language)</a><a href=\"#validation-education-errata-in-the-printed-volume\">Errata in the printed volume</a><a href=\"#validation-education-check-6-hand-coding-a-stratified-sample-score-education-gold-py-drawn-not-yet-coded\">Check 6 — hand-coding a stratified sample (score_education_gold.py) — drawn, not yet coded</a><a href=\"#validation-education-what-these-checks-are-blind-to\">What these checks are blind to</a><a href=\"#validation-education-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</a></nav>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Check</th>\n<th>What it reaches</th>\n<th>Status, in the check's own words</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1. The ladder against the state's own list of school kinds</td>\n<td>the rungs</td>\n<td>passed, with two documented gaps, neither a defect</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2. Is <code>pok.</code> a rung, or a separate kind of thing?</td>\n<td>the continuation school</td>\n<td>passed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3. Table 34 against <code>education_complete</code></td>\n<td>the completion flag</td>\n<td><strong>FAILED</strong>; recorded as <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a>; ruled 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4. Continuation : full-time vocational</td>\n<td>how completely <code>pok.</code> is written down</td>\n<td>inconclusive as a placebo test; informative as a level comparison</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5. The Czech-language benchmark</td>\n<td>how selective rung 2 was</td>\n<td>descriptive; no pass/fail</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6. Hand-coding a stratified sample</td>\n<td>the tokeniser</td>\n<td>drawn, not yet coded</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Status: run 2026-09-07.</strong> Two tests confirm the scheme, one <strong>fails</strong> it, one is inconclusive-but-informative, one is\ndescriptive. The failure is recorded as <a href=\"#decisions\">D-53</a>. It changed an emitted column and wanted a decision, not a patch;\nthe author gave it on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>): 8 or more is complete, a number below 8 is <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code> (<code>education.py</code> 2.2.0).</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-the-source\">The source</h2>\n<p><strong><em>Österreichische Statistik</em>, XCIII. Band, 1. Heft — <em>Statistik der Unterrichtsanstalten in den im\nReichsrate vertretenen Königreichen und Ländern für das Jahr 1908/1909</em></strong> (k.k. Statistische\nZentralkommission, Wien 1912). See <a href=\"#sources\"><code>DATA_SOURCES.md</code></a> #21.</p>\n<p>Why it is the right source, and why it was not available before:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The ladder in <code>education.py</code> was built from <strong>two secondary works</strong> — <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"moore_2020\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Moore (2020)</a> for the general ladder, Lassnigg\n  (2015) for the vocational branch. Neither counts schools. Moore describes the law; Lassnigg's own quantitative series\n  begins in <strong>1924</strong>, in the Republic of Austria, on territory this sample does not cover.\n  <a href=\"#education\"><code>EDUCATION_LADDER.md</code></a> §5 nominated this class of source by name as the missing filler.</li>\n<li>It is the administration's <strong>own classification</strong> of its own schools, contemporaneous with the years this cohort was\n  at school, tabulated for Böhmen / Mähren / Schlesien and split by <em>Unterrichtssprache</em> — so the benchmark can be\n  restricted to Czech-language institutions rather than to all of Cisleithania.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Held here:</strong> a 279-page image-only scan, merged from 15 ÖNB download parts, at\n<code>library/education/OeStat-1912_Bd-XCIII-1_Statistik-der-Unterrichtsanstalten-1908-09.pdf</code> (gitignored). Folio →\nPDF-page map in <code>reference/education/unterricht_page_index.csv</code> (<code>build_page_index.py</code>). ⚠ Einleitung <strong>X–XI</strong> and\ntable page <strong>15</strong> were not downloaded.</p>\n<p><strong>Transcribed to</strong> three wide CSVs shaped like the printed pages — <code>unterricht_t34_volksschulen.csv</code>,\n<code>unterricht_t20_gewerbeschulen.csv</code>, <code>unterricht_t19_handelslehranstalten.csv</code> — and gated by\n<code>check_unterricht_transcription.py</code> (<strong>27/27</strong>).</p>\n<details><summary>Why the transcription needs a gate, and why the gate works</summary>\n\n<p>The gate is the same guard as <code>check_atlas_parties.py</code> and exists for the same reason: a row-offset in a table read off a scan leaves no grammatical trace. It works because the volume over-determines itself — every table prints the parts <i>and</i> the roll-ups <i>and</i> the column totals, and in Table 34 the eight class columns must also sum across each row.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-1-the-ladder-against-the-state-s-own-list-of-school-kinds-run-taxonomy\">Check 1 — the ladder against the state's own list of school kinds (<code>run_taxonomy</code>)</h2>\n<p><strong>Status: passed, with two documented gaps, neither a defect.</strong></p>\n<p>21 rungs in <code>INSTITUTIONS</code>, 17 matched to a school kind the volume enumerates.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Four rungs the volume does not list</strong>: <code>illiterate</code>, <code>no_school</code>, <code>secondary</code>, <code>cadet</code>. Correct — the\n  Kadettenschule is a military establishment outside the k.k. Ministerium für Kultus und Unterricht, illiteracy is a\n  census category rather than an institution, and <code>secondary</code> is the parser's own \"unspecified\" bucket.</li>\n<li><strong>Two school kinds with no token</strong>: <code>Handwerkerschule</code> and <code>Notschule</code>.</li>\n<li><code>Handwerkerschule</code> is folded into <code>trade</code>. The volume counts <strong>13</strong> in the whole empire, 8 of them in Böhmen — the\n    merge costs almost nothing.</li>\n<li><code>Notschule</code> (the emergency one-teacher school) has none, and needs none <em>here</em>: <strong>1</strong> in the Czech lands against\n    <strong>379</strong> in Cisleithania, of which Tirol alone has <strong>277</strong>. It is an Alpine and Galician phenomenon, not a Bohemian\n    one. ⚠ This is contingent on the sample, not on the parser: a study of Tirolean or Krain births would need the\n    token.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-2-is-pok-a-rung-or-a-separate-kind-of-thing-run-continuation\">Check 2 — is <code>pok.</code> a rung, or a separate kind of thing? (<code>run_continuation</code>)</h2>\n<p><strong>Status: passed. The <code>pok.</code> decision is confirmed by the administration's own filing.</strong></p>\n<p>p. XX splits the vocational branch into <em>a)</em> Fachschulen für gewerbliche Hauptgruppen, <em>b)</em> Fachschulen für einzelne\ngewerbliche Zweige, <em>c)</em> Handwerkerschulen, and <em>d)</em> <strong>gewerbliche Fortbildungs- und Zeichenschulen</strong> — a separate\ncategory. p. XVI does the same commercially: 24 höhere Handelsschulen + 115 kommerzielle <em>Tagesschulen</em> + <strong>168\nkaufmännische Fortbildungsschulen</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Land</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">full-time Anstalten</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Fortbild. Anstalten</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">full-time Schüler</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Fortbild. Schüler</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Fortbild. % of pupils</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Böhmen</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">102</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">504</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">9,672</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">50,836</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>84.0</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mähren</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">27</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">173</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,645</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">14,278</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">84.4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Schlesien</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">47</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">639</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,956</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">86.1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Im ganzen</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">327</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,200</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">24,089</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">128,462</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">84.2</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Keeping <code>continuation</code> off the ordinal (<code>INSTITUTIONS</code> ordinal <code>None</code>) agrees with the source. The v1.0.0 reading —\n<code>pok.</code> as <em>Upper secondary</em>, level with <code>gym.</code> — would have put the <strong>largest and least selective</strong> school kind in the\nempire at the top of the ladder.</p>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-3-table-34-against-education-complete-run-klassen-fails\">Check 3 — Table 34 against <code>education_complete</code> (<code>run_klassen</code>) ⚠ <strong>FAILS</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Status: FAILED. Recorded as <a href=\"#decisions\">D-53</a>; ruled on 2026-11-21 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-272\">D-272</a>): the flag no longer judges a number below 8.</strong></p>\n<p>Table 34 counts allgemeine Volksschulen by <strong>number of ascending classes</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>classes</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">1</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">2</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">3</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">4</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">5</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">6</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">7</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>8</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cisleithania</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,940</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,433</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,372</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,914</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,624</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">620</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">62</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>10</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Böhmen</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,112</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,703</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">951</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">562</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,114</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">97</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Czech lands</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,108</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,639</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,412</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">783</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,562</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">191</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">14</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><code>education.py</code> scores completion for a bare Volksschule against <strong>8</strong> (<code>education.py</code>, \"the standard here is always\nthe full eight years (Moore p. 30)\"). An eight-class Volksschule existed <strong>ten times in all Cisleithania and twice in\nthe Czech lands</strong>, against 1,114 five-class schools in Böhmen alone.</p>\n<p>Among the <strong>11,986</strong> Czech-lands-born records with <code>education_top == \"elementary\"</code> and a stated year (the run of\n2026-09-07; the stated years are in the fold below):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>3,894</strong> records are scored <em>complete</em> against a school form that barely existed;</li>\n<li><strong>3,137</strong> records reading <code>ob. 5</code> — the modal <strong>full</strong> Bohemian Volksschule — are scored <em>incomplete</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The defect is a conflation of units.</strong> Moore's eight years are a <em>legal obligation spanning institutions</em>\n(Volksschule 5 + Bürgerschule 3); Table 34's classes are an <em>institutional form</em>. A bare <code>ob. N</code> in <code>Vzdělání</code> does not\nsay which of the two it records, and <code>education_complete</code> currently resolves that ambiguity by assumption.</p>\n<p>This is the \"rule narrower than its source\" shape the project has hit before (<code>ranks</code> 1.4.0, <code>occupations</code> 1.1.0,\n<code>education</code> 1.0.0). Note what is <strong>not</strong> affected: <code>education_ord</code>, <code>education_top</code>, <code>education_track</code> and\n<code>education_years_elementary</code> are all untouched by this. Only the completion flag moves.</p>\n<details><summary>The stated years, by completion flag (the run of 2026-09-07)</summary>\n\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>stated years</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th><th>6</th><th>7</th><th>8</th><th>9</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><code>complete = False</code></td><td>154</td><td>925</td><td>1,772</td><td>1,377</td><td><b>3,137</b></td><td>590</td><td>137</td><td>–</td><td>–</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>complete = True</code></td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td>3,890</td><td>4</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n\n<p>The same counts on the current <code>data/final</code> are the sizes in the method's <i>Open for the author</i> table.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-4-continuation-full-time-vocational-run-composition\">Check 4 — continuation : full-time vocational (<code>run_composition</code>)</h2>\n<p><strong>Status: inconclusive as a placebo test; informative as a level comparison.</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">ratio</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Records (Czech-lands-born, non-empty <code>Vzdělání</code>, n=86,858) — A:B</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>0.86</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Benchmark, Czech lands (pupils)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>5.33</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Benchmark, Galizien (placebo)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.41</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Benchmark, Tirol (placebo)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.32</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>where A = names a continuation school (8,236), B = names a full-time vocational school (9,549), overlap 796. Built\nfrom <code>education_institutions</code> rather than the ordinal, so a record naming both a Gymnasium and a Handelsschule is not\nsilently dropped.</p>\n<p><strong>What the levels say is worth keeping.</strong> The Czech lands had <strong>5.3</strong> continuation pupils per full-time vocational\npupil; the records name them at <strong>0.86</strong> to one — roughly <strong>6× fewer</strong> — and the gap survives every reasonable\nreconstruction of the two sets. The likeliest reading is that <code>pok.</code> is <strong>under-recorded</strong>: the continuation school was\ncompulsory, part-time and unremarkable, and a man setting down his schooling names the trade school he chose rather than\nthe evening classes he was obliged to sit.</p>\n<p>Part of the gap is also flow-vs-stock and part is selection into the Legion, and this design cannot apportion it.\n<strong>Consequence for the paper:</strong> <code>education_apprentice</code> (6.6 % of records) is a\n<strong>lower bound</strong> on apprenticeship, not a rate. A specification treating it as an exhaustive category will understate\nthe group.</p>\n<details><summary>Why the placebo cannot separate</summary>\n\n<p><b>The placebo does not separate, and on inspection it cannot.</b> The benchmark ratio varies across crownlands for reasons unrelated to how well a crownland describes this sample — Tirol's low ratio comes from its many Fachschulen, not from any affinity with Czech births. The placebo is not exchangeable with the treatment, so its ordering carries no information. Recorded so nobody re-runs it expecting one.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-5-the-czech-language-benchmark-and-how-selective-rung-2-was-run-language\">Check 5 — the Czech-language benchmark, and how selective rung 2 was (<code>run_language</code>)</h2>\n<p><strong>Status: descriptive; no pass/fail.</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Land</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Bürgerschulen</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">deutsch</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">čecho-slavisch</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Czech %</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Böhmen</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">608</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">234</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">374</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">61.5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mähren</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">223</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">90</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">133</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">59.6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Schlesien</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">36</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">31</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">11.1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Cisleithania: 1,266 Bürgerschulen, 511 čecho-slavisch (40.4%). The Bürgerschule was <strong>1,266 of 22,241</strong> public\nelementary institutions — <strong>5.7%</strong>. Rung 2 of the ladder is a <em>selective</em> step, not the ordinary continuation of rung 1,\nand should be read that way.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-errata-in-the-printed-volume\">Errata in the printed volume</h2>\n<p>Both were found by the checks, not assumed. Each is decided by a <strong>second</strong> arithmetic path, because \"the source is\nwrong\" is otherwise unfalsifiable and would let any bad read pass.</p>\n<p>There are two: a roll-up in Table 20 (<em>Tirol und Vorarlberg</em>) that disagrees with its own crownland rows, and a figure\nin the Einleitung's prose (p. XXXII) that disagrees with Table 34. In both, the rows and the tables win.</p>\n<details><summary>The two errata, and the arithmetic that decides each</summary>\n\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>What</th><th>Which side wins, and why</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Table 20 (p. XX), <i>Tirol und Vorarlberg</i></td><td>Tirol 30 + Vorarlberg 13 gewerbliche Fortbildungsschulen, rolled up to <b>42</b>; and 52 + 14 Anstalten rolled up to <b>65</b></td><td>The <b>crownland rows</b>. Every other cell of the same roll-up adds exactly (Lehrkräfte 83+53=136, Schüler 1.839+447=2.286, Zusammen 250+60=310 and 3.237+516=3.753), and the empire total of 1.200 Anstalten agrees with the rows, not the roll-up</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Einleitung p. XXXII (prose)</td><td>\"22.341 öffentliche Volksschulen\"</td><td><b>22,241</b>. Table 34 sums to 1,266 + 20,975 = 22,241, and the Einleitung's <i>own</i> summary table on p. I also prints 22.241. The prose figure is one hundred too high</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n\n</details>\n\n<p>The transcription follows the printed page in both cases; the errata are declared in\n<code>check_unterricht_transcription.py</code> (<code>KNOWN_SOURCE_ERRATA</code>) and reported separately from failures.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-check-6-hand-coding-a-stratified-sample-score-education-gold-py-drawn-not-yet-coded\">Check 6 — hand-coding a stratified sample (<code>score_education_gold.py</code>) — <strong>drawn, not yet coded</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Status: instrument built 2026-09-07, sample drawn, worksheets empty.</strong> Both worksheets\n(<code>reference/education/education_gold/calibration/</code> and <code>certification/</code>) were still uncoded on 2026-11-20.</p>\n<p>The five checks above test the <strong>ladder</strong> — whether the rungs are the school kinds the state operated. None of them\ntests the <strong>tokeniser</strong>: whether <code>education.py</code> reads out of <code>ob. 5 mě. 3 pok. 3</code> what a Czech reader reads. No\nexternal source can, because the strings are this archive's own shorthand. Only a person can, and this is the\ninstrument for it.</p>\n<p><strong>Design.</strong> 300 records, disproportionately stratified by <em>risk</em> rather than frequency, split into a <strong>calibration</strong>\nhalf (iterate freely) and a sealed <strong><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-certification-en\" data-gl=\"certification\">certification</a></strong> half (coded once, reported):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>stratum</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">in frame</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">drawn</th>\n<th>why it is over-sampled</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>plain</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">71,622</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">90</td>\n<td>one school, no complication — the bulk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>multi_rung</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">17,341</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">60</td>\n<td>the itinerary and the <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-51\">D-51</a> tie-break</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>elem_with_years</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">14,516</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">60</td>\n<td>the population <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-53\">D-53</a> is about</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>imputed_floor</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,112</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">30</td>\n<td><code>educ_top</code> inferred, not named</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>unparsed</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">952</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">40</td>\n<td>non-empty, parser returned nothing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rung0</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">449</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">20</td>\n<td>small and high-consequence</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Three properties that decide whether the number means anything:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The worksheet is blind.</strong> It carries the raw string and nothing else — not the parser's answer, not even the\n  stratum, since <code>unparsed</code> would tell the coder the machine had already failed. Showing the machine's answer measures\n  assent, not accuracy.</li>\n<li><strong>The coder names institutions, never a rung.</strong> The rung is derived afterwards from their institutions using the\n  parser's own <code>INSTITUTIONS</code> table. So a disagreement is unambiguously about <em>reading</em>; a rung that differs while the\n  institutions agree would be a bug in the ranking code, and the scorer reports that cell separately and says it should\n  be zero.</li>\n<li><strong>The <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-headline-en\" data-gl=\"headline\">headline</a> is reweighted</strong> to the true stratum sizes. An unweighted mean over a sample that is 13 % <code>unparsed</code>\n  records describes a population that does not exist.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A blank cell counts as <em>not coded</em>, not as agreement; blanks are excluded and reported, because a half-filled worksheet\notherwise yields a confident wrong number.</p>\n<p><strong>Already visible from the draw, before anyone codes:</strong> 952 non-empty strings parse to nothing (0.9 %), and the tail\ncontains real dictionary gaps rather than noise — <code>negr.</code> (negramotný, i.e. <code>illiterate</code>), <code>bez</code> (<code>no_school</code>),\n<code>lesní ak.</code>, <code>řemesl.š.</code>, <code>st.tech. 2</code>, <code>tech. 4sem.</code>. The patterns require <code>negram</code> and <code>bez vzděl</code> respectively, so\nboth abbreviations fall through. These are exactly the kind of miss the instrument exists to find systematically rather\nthan anecdotally.</p>\n<details><summary>Running it</summary>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">python</span> <span class=\"n\">utils</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">reference_tools</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">education</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">draw_education_sample</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">py</span>          <span class=\"c1\"># reproducible, seed 1910</span>\n<span class=\"n\">python</span> <span class=\"n\">utils</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">reference_tools</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">education</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">score_education_gold</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">py</span> <span class=\"n\">calibration</span>\n</pre></div>\n\n\n\n\n<p>Instructions for the coder, in Czech, with the closed token list: <code>education_gold/NAVOD.md</code>.</p>\n\n</details>\n\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-what-these-checks-are-blind-to\">What these checks are blind to</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Hungary — the reason <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-08\">D-08</a> stays open.</strong> The volume is <em>\"in den im Reichsrate vertretenen Königreichen und\n  Ländern\"</em>: Cisleithania <strong>by definition</strong>. Every test above restricts to Czech-lands births and the ~10,500\n  Slovakia-born records are excluded, so nothing here establishes that a Transleithanian <code>mě.</code> is the Cisleithanian\n  one. The fix is the Eötvös 1868 and Apponyi 1907 school laws and the Magyar statistical series, not another pass over\n  these tables.</li>\n<li><strong>Flow versus stock.</strong> The volume counts pupils enrolled in 1908/09; the field records the schooling of men born\n  mostly 1875–1900, observed years later. No test here treats a benchmark share as an expected sample share, and Check 4\n  documents what that costs.</li>\n<li><strong>Institutions versus pupils.</strong> Tables 20 and 34 count schools in some columns and pupils in others. A ratio of school\n  counts is not a ratio of people.</li>\n<li><strong>One year only.</strong> 1908/09 is a single cross-section near the <em>end</em> of the cohort's schooling. The Volksschule class\n  distribution in particular was changing (Table 34 is a stock at end-1909), so it understates how few eight-class\n  schools existed when the older birth cohorts were at school — which if anything strengthens Check 3.</li>\n<li><strong>Attendance is still not reached at the individual level.</strong> Table 39 defines a <em>Schulbesuchserleichterung</em> — schools\n  where \"die Kinder ganzer Ortschaften oder Weiler die Schule <strong>wöchentlich nur ein bis dreimal</strong> besuchen\" — and counts\n  them, but <strong>by Land</strong>, not by Bezirk. It narrows <code>EDUCATION_LADDER.md</code> §5's attendance-vs-enrolment caveat; it does\n  not close it, and gives no okres covariate.</li>\n<li><strong>The two missing pages.</strong> Einleitung X–XI (Gymnasium detail) and table page 15 were not downloaded. Nothing above\n  depends on them.</li>\n<li><strong>The tokeniser, until Check 6 is actually coded.</strong> The sample is drawn and the scorer works, but the worksheets are\n  empty. Everything above tests the ladder, not the reading of the strings.</li>\n<li><strong>The transcription is three tables, not forty-one.</strong> Tables 21–33 and 35–41 are in the scan and unread. Table 20's\n  per-institution lists (pp. 114–175) carry a <em>Standort</em> for every school and are geocodable to 1910 okres through\n  <code>settlements_1910</code> — the route to an okres-level schooling covariate, and a second-wave project, not this one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"validation-education-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</h2>\n<details><summary>What changed on this page, and when</summary>\n\n<p><b>The page.</b> In the docs pass (2026-11-20) it became the <i>How sure</i> section of <i>Education</i>. The checks' runs, dates and results stay in the checks; the passages below moved here word for word.</p>\n\n<p><b>Before this check.</b> \"Until this, education was the one major constructed variable with <b>no external check at all</b>: it appeared in <a href=\"#validation-register\"><code>VALIDATION.md</code></a> only under §3, \"What none of them reach\".\"</p>\n\n</details><nav class=\"seealso\"><span class=\"sal\">See also</span><a href=\"#education\" onclick=\"show('education')\"><b>Education ladder</b><span>The 1869 Austrian school ladder — and why the apprentices&#x27; continuation school is not a rung on it.</span></a><a href=\"#validation-register\" onclick=\"show('validation-register')\"><b>Validation register</b><span>Every check, and what each one is blind to.</span></a><a href=\"#decisions\" onclick=\"show('decisions')\"><b>Decisions</b><span>Register of every judgement call, with a link to the argument.</span></a></nav></div></section>");
